      "value": "@{63691297469f06772579fe6f|full_name}: Not entirely. I recreated the animator again from scratch and got the same behavior, so its not some weird interal thing that just broke.\n\nI'm currently in the process of adding things one by one and test and see what is actually causing these issues. I managed to add a lot of the base features of the Face Tracking without running into any freezes. \n\nMy best guess at the moment is, that this caused the freezes:\n\nControlling a VRChat Tracking controlled Blend Shape with a network synced float with a blend tree. (For example the Blink Blendshape, or a mouth viseme)\n\nI had VRChat blinking for my Avatar with the Blendshape vrc.blink\n\nAnd i also had a 1D Blend Tree Blend between an Animation where vrc.blink was 0, and one where vrc.blink was 100, depending on how sad of an expression I made.\n\nSame thing with vrc.o Viseme.\n\nVRChat plays the visemes depending on the Audio, but i also had my Face Tracking Blend Tree control vrc.o depending on how i funnel my lips. \n\nThese 2 Features are the only ones i didn't add to my animator yet, and so far no freezes. I will get to test it further the next few days.\n\nI also still have a copy of the \"broken\" animator, in case you'd like to have a look at it or something ^^'",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
